WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.953 --> 00:00:16.485
I downstairs and knocked on the door to Josh's apartment.

2
00:00:16.505 --> 00:00:20.748
"Hi," I blurted out when Josh came to the door.

3
00:00:20.768 --> 00:00:23.551
"Can I see your dad's one-way mirror?"

4
00:00:24.832 --> 00:00:27.314
Mr. Chen appeared behind Josh with a smile.

5
00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.676
"Follow me," he said.

6
00:00:31.604 --> 00:00:33.325
Josh, Jenny, and I followed Mr.

7
00:00:33.405 --> 00:00:35.487
Chen into a small room off the hall.

8
00:00:37.568 --> 00:00:40.250
It was the first time I had ever been inside Mr.

9
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.411
Chen's magic room.

10
00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:44.032
It was amazing!

11
00:00:44.953 --> 00:00:48.575
The room was filled with all sorts of magic props and supplies.

12
00:00:49.496 --> 00:00:55.140
There were top hats, colored boxes, packs of cards, and gold coins.

13
00:00:56.581 --> 00:01:01.064
There were balls of different sizes, colorful feathers, even a large saw.

14
00:01:02.376 --> 00:01:06.199
Mr. Chen led me over to something that looked like a small window.

15
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.944
Josh had told me what a one-way mirror was, but I still had questions.

16
00:01:11.964 --> 00:01:16.588
"I don't understand exactly how it works," I told Mr.

17
00:01:16.648 --> 00:01:24.034
Chen. "Well," he replied, "imagine one person in a bright room and another person in a dark room.

18
00:01:24.454 --> 00:01:25.775
The mirror is between them."

19
00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:29.979
"Okay," I said, picturing that in my mind.

20
00:01:29.999 --> 00:01:31.500
"Now what?"

21
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.161
"When the person in the bright room looks at the mirror, all he sees is himself," Mr.

22
00:01:37.241 --> 00:01:38.042
Chen went on.

23
00:01:38.062 --> 00:01:40.843
"Got it," I said.

24
00:01:42.203 --> 00:01:43.303
Mr. Chen grinned.

25
00:01:43.323 --> 00:01:48.425
"But when the person in the dark room looks at the mirror, he sees something different.

26
00:01:48.805 --> 00:01:50.805
He sees the other person through the glass!"

27
00:01:50.825 --> 00:01:53.766
"Wow," I said.

28
00:01:54.527 --> 00:01:56.147
By now I was thinking hard.

29
00:01:56.827 --> 00:01:59.188
I was thinking so hard, my brain hurt.

30
00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.482
"I think I know how to make a magic thinking box," I said finally.

31
00:02:05.502 --> 00:02:08.484
"How?" asked Jenny.

32
00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:11.666
"Can I borrow your one-way mirror, Mr.

33
00:02:11.706 --> 00:02:12.907
Chen?" I asked.

34
00:02:12.927 --> 00:02:15.648
"Sure," said Mr.

35
00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:18.350
Chen. "I actually have an extra one."

36
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.072
He picked up a smaller one-way mirror and handed it to me.

37
00:02:23.092 --> 00:02:29.876
"Now I just need scissors, a flashlight, and a cardboard box," I said.

38
00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.221
I ran upstairs and got some scissors.

39
00:02:37.203 --> 00:02:39.664
I also got Molly so she could join in the fun.

40
00:02:40.845 --> 00:02:45.729
Jenny found a flashlight, and Josh got an old box from the Green Apple Supermarket.

41
00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.952
First I cut a hole out of the cardboard box with the scissors.

42
00:02:55.935 --> 00:02:58.857
It was just a tiny bit smaller than the one-way mirror.

43
00:03:00.318 --> 00:03:02.480
Next I fitted the mirror into the hole.

44
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.241
"Now," I said, "who wants to try the magic thinking box first?"

45
00:03:10.261 --> 00:03:12.982
"Me!" cried Molly.

46
00:03:13.002 --> 00:03:14.742
"Let me try it!"

47
00:03:14.762 --> 00:03:16.923
"Okay," I said.

48
00:03:16.943 --> 00:03:19.164
"Put the box over your head."

49
00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:22.685
Molly put the box over her head.

50
00:03:22.705 --> 00:03:27.146
"It's dark in here," she said in a muffled voice.

51
00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:30.427
"I can't see anything at all."

52
00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:32.287
"Just a minute!"

53
00:03:32.607 --> 00:03:33.908
I handed her the flashlight.

54
00:03:33.928 --> 00:03:39.470
"Now turn this on and shine it into the box," I told her.

55
00:03:41.151 --> 00:03:43.672
Molly turned on the flashlight inside the box.

56
00:03:44.593 --> 00:03:46.414
Then I turned off the light in the room.

57
00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.155
"Can you see us?"

58
00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:50.336
I asked Molly.

59
00:03:50.356 --> 00:03:53.097
"No," said Molly.

60
00:03:53.117 --> 00:03:55.959
"All I can see is myself in the mirror."

61
00:03:55.979 --> 00:03:58.200
"We can see you though!"

62
00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.261
cried Josh.

63
00:03:59.281 --> 00:04:00.922
"It works!"

64
00:04:01.342 --> 00:04:01.982
I shouted.

65
00:04:02.002 --> 00:04:05.004
"No, it doesn't," said Molly.

66
00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.903
"You can see me, but you can't tell what I'm thinking!"

67
00:04:10.244 --> 00:04:11.985
I looked at her face through the glass.

68
00:04:12.706 --> 00:04:14.768
Her eyes were bright, and she was grinning.

69
00:04:14.788 --> 00:04:17.650
"She looks excited," I thought.

70
00:04:18.311 --> 00:04:20.953
But she also looked a little suspicious of my box.

71
00:04:21.914 --> 00:04:25.377
"You're thinking that you want me to put on the box," I said.

72
00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:28.620
"So that you can tell what I'm thinking."

73
00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:30.861
Molly gasped.

74
00:04:31.902 --> 00:04:33.544
"That's right, Iggy!"

75
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.581
She yanked the box off her head and looked at me.

76
00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:39.122
"Iggy," she said.

77
00:04:39.142 --> 00:04:40.603
"You did it!

78
00:04:40.883 --> 00:04:44.464
You invented a magic thinking box!"

79
00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:45.184
"Way to go!"

80
00:04:45.725 --> 00:04:47.986
said Josh, giving me a high five.

81
00:04:49.046 --> 00:04:49.606
I grinned.

82
00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:53.008
My magic thinking box actually worked!
